@startuml seq-amadla-run

title amadla run — Execute the Pipeline DAG

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor #444

actor "User" as user
participant "cmd/" as cmd
participant "toolconfig/" as toolconfig
participant "dag/" as dag
participant "Filesystem" as fs
participant "Tool CLI\n(raise, lay, enjoin, weaver, ...)" as tool

== Config load & enrichment ==

user -> cmd : amadla run [entity-dir] [--dry-run]
cmd -> toolconfig : Load(--config path or\n~/.config/amadla/tools.hery)
toolconfig -> fs : Read tools.hery
toolconfig --> cmd : Config (tools list)
cmd -> toolconfig : EnrichWithInfo(cfg, InfoCache)
toolconfig -> fs : Read ~/.cache/amadla/tool-info.json
toolconfig -> tool : <tool> info -o json\n(only on cache miss or binary mtime change,\nonly for tools without supports in config)
tool --> toolconfig : name, version, supports
toolconfig -> fs : Write refreshed cache
toolconfig --> cmd : supports filled in\n(enrichment failures are silent)
cmd -> cmd : buildToolMap\n(entity type URI → tool)

== DAG build ==

cmd -> fs : ReadDir(entity-dir),\nread each *.hery file (non-recursive)
cmd -> dag : Add(node) per document\n(URI = _type, edges = _requires)
cmd -> dag : Levels() — Kahn's algorithm
dag --> cmd : Parallel execution tiers

== Dry run: --dry-run ==

cmd --> user : Numbered execution order on stdout\n([parallel] marks concurrent tiers), exit 0

== Execution (tier by tier) ==

cmd -> toolconfig : ResolvePath(tool) per entity\n(explicit path, else PATH lookup)
toolconfig --> cmd : Binary path
cmd -> tool : Spawn tool — entity JSON on stdin\n+ AMADLA_ENTITY env var\n(one goroutine per entity in the tier)
tool --> user : Tool stdout/stderr pass through
tool --> cmd : Exit code
cmd --> user : exit 0 when all tiers succeed

== Errors ==

user -> cmd : cycle in _requires
cmd --> user : "DAG resolution failed: circular\n_requires reference detected" on stderr, exit 1
user -> cmd : entity type with no registered tool
cmd --> user : warning on stderr, entity skipped,\nrun continues
user -> cmd : tool exits non-zero
cmd --> user : "tool <name> failed for <uri>" on stderr, exit 1\n(other entities in the same tier still finish;\nonly the first error is reported)

@enduml
